    "body": "Hi @rniwa, can you point to any inaccurate sections in the spec? It's not meant to be offensive, just factual. We're happy to correct any errors.\n\nThere's a long history of introduction sections that explain to web developers how to use a feature and the consequences of using it; remember that the HTML spec is not only for implementers. You can see other examples in e.g.:\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/introduction.html#a-quick-introduction-to-html\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#introduction-3\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#introduction-4\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#introduction-13\n\nand others.\n\nI don't think we'll remove these sections or the content in them, but as I said, I'm happy to correct any factual inaccuracies (\"bugs\") you find.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
